Mini Vector AML baseline

This compact implementation follows the non-graph open-source memory workflow
of mem0 (https://github.com/mem0ai/mem0). The upstream project is licensed under
Apache License 2.0. Its license is preserved in third_party/mem0/LICENSE and
includes the original notice: Copyright [2023] [Taranjeet Singh].

Attribution reference: mem0 commit 47a69e1e72dc562b6fdd49a9ef892229afc7508a.
That reference identifies the locally inspected upstream snapshot; it does not
claim that this repository is an unmodified checkout of that commit.

Changes from the upstream workflow include a compact synchronous Python API,
SQLite persistence, exact vector scanning, FTS5 BM25 reranking, ADD-only fact
extraction, and an AML-specific authenticated Add/Search adapter with atomic
batch ingestion, durable idempotency, exact user isolation, and Qwen embeddings.
This repository does not distribute mem0's full source tree or benchmark data.

Publication packaging adds documentation, examples, provenance and attribution.
Runtime source and the bundled tests are copied unchanged from the baseline
deployment archive identified in BASELINE_MANIFEST.json.
